Package: protux
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: all
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: FrankMncrf <57369835+FrankMncrf@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: bash, rclone, fuse3, systemd, gawk
Recommends: python3-pyqt6, pkexec | policykit-1, libsecret-tools, libnotify-bin, dbus-user-session
Suggests: zenity | kdialog
Homepage: https://github.com/FrankMncrf/Protux
Description: Proton Drive client for Linux: mount your drive as a folder
 Protux mounts Proton Drive as a normal folder with rclone and a systemd
 user service, and keeps it working: setup wizard, system tray icon,
 2FA re-login prompts when the session expires, two-password accounts,
 and no login loops that get the account rate-limited (HTTP 429).
 .
 Debian 13 and Ubuntu 24.04 ship an rclone without the Proton Drive
 backend: install rclone >= 1.64 from rclone.org.
 .
 Unofficial; not affiliated with Proton AG.
